   },
   "title": "How to use · v1.0.0",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use · v1.0.0\n\n**What it does:** Stable Diffusion 3.5 Large text to image from one fp8 checkpoint, 20 steps, 1024x1024 by default. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Your inputs** (green group):\n   - **Prompt**: describe the picture. SD3.5 can write short text: put the words in quotes.\n   - **Negative prompt**: what to avoid. Empty in the template.\n   - **Size**: pick the shape; megapixels 1 = 1024x1024 (16:9 = 1360x768). Leave \"multiple\" at 16.\n   - **Steps** (20) and **CFG** (4.01): the template's values.\n   - **Seed**: fixed at 24112026, so the first Run gives the README picture. Type a new number (or set \"control after generate\" to randomize) for a new picture; Run with nothing changed does nothing.\n2. **Model**: the loader must show `sd3.5_large_fp8_scaled.safetensors` from the Downloads note. Nothing to change.\n3. **Prompt**: nothing to change; the text comes from group 1.\n4. **Sampling**: euler / sgm_uniform, from the template. More pictures per run: `batch_size` on the **Empty picture** node here.\n5. Press **Run**. The picture is saved by the **Result** node to `output/SD3.5/`.\n\n**What to expect:** about 23 s per 1024x1024 picture at 20 steps on the lab's 24 GB card (RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell), 24 s when the model has to load first (file already in the RAM cache). 16:9 (1360x768) took 22 s. In 12 and 10 GiB VRAM budgets the same pictures took 24-25 s (fresh instance, load included) and came out byte-identical.\n\n**CFG box shows 4.0:** the box rounds to one decimal; the value inside is 4.01 (checked in the prompt ComfyUI sends).\n\n**Text in the picture:** the sign \"FRESH BREAD\" came out spelled right on 3 of 3 seeds; smaller extra lettering (on an awning) came out as scribble.\n\n**Tested on:** ComfyUI 0.45.3, RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB, 2026-11-24. Not verified on a 12 GB card.\n"
   ]
  },
